+# KMS Lockdown & Hardened Builder Instructions
+
+This document outlines steps to apply Terraform and harden builder hosts for cosign KMS keys.
+
+1) Review Terraform (ops/infra/terraform/*)
+ - Ensure aws_account_id, github_owner, github_repo and audit_s3_bucket are set in terraform.tfvars (use terraform.tfvars.example).
+ - Use remote state backend (S3/GCS) with encryption and access control.
+
+2) Run plan and get CloudSec sign-off
+ - terraform init
+ - terraform plan -var-file=terraform.tfvars -out=tfplan
+ - Share tfplan with CloudSec for review (do not apply until approved)
+
+3) Apply plan in controlled window
+ - terraform apply tfplan
+ - Verify KMS key alias, IAM OIDC role, and CloudTrail log delivery to the audit bucket.
+
+4) Harden builders
+ - Use ephemeral VMs for wheel builds with no persistent credentials.
+ - Enable OS hardening (unattended upgrades, minimal packages).
+ - Restrict network egress (only permit GitHub & required artifact stores).
+ - Capture builder provenance: git commit SHA, container image digest, build logs, and checksums.
+
+5) Validation
+ - Trigger production_builder_hardened.sh on a hardened runner; confirm checksums and provenance are generated and wheels are cosign-signed via KMS.
+ - Inspect CloudTrail entries for KMS Sign operations.
